From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Leiter <8675906+MaxLeiter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:19:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spread arguments in calls and new

f(...a, b), obj.m(...a), f?.(...a) and new C(...a). The arguments of
such a call are gathered in one array literal. The interpreter passes
its elements on as the call's bound arguments, so interpreted callees
still run in the same interpreter loop; compiled code turns it into the
argument array.

eval(...args) is an indirect eval.

This includes upstream's cf04a1c85 ("fix: Array spread throws TypeError
on non-iterable, null, or undefined targets"), so that spreading
something that is not iterable throws a TypeError instead of passing
nothing.

